  "findings": [
    "Navigation functions, but remaining stalls are reproducible in the development simulator.",
    "Ordinary navigation reached 287 ms of React work. Rapid navigation with CPU profiling reached 424 ms. Navigation after a furniture save reached 258 ms with React profiling only.",
    "The lightweight rapid-navigation run still had a 1293 ms JS animation-frame gap, so the observed stalls are not solely caused by the CPU/React profiler. This is not a direct native display-frame or finger-to-screen measurement.",
    "In the largest post-save navigation commit, all four PetStage components updated and room-action menus rebuilt. Hidden stages received changed onVisitHomeRoom, onSendCatToRoom, storedItems and onBedRemove props despite unchanged furniture. This is a concrete follow-up target; no fix attempted in this testing-only task."
  ],
